  "gold_solution": "```python\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"Transportation_Problem\")\n    m.setParam(\"TimeLimit\", 300)  # Set time limit to 300 seconds\n\n    # Data\n    sources = list(range(10))  # S0..S9\n    destinations = list(range(13))  # D0..D12\n\n    supplies = [52, 53, 73, 83, 65, 91, 91, 27, 68, 55]\n    demands = [44, 33, 72, 65, 16, 56, 41, 43, 28, 60, 47, 67, 21]\n\n    # Cost matrix: rows correspond to sources S0..S9, columns to destinations D0..D12\n    costs = [\n        [ 11.82,  14.20,  25.96,  23.62,  16.40,  27.11,  23.96,  26.74,   8.89,  23.61,  28.41,  15.77,  16.73],  # S0\n        [ 15.28,   7.49,  29.95,  17.44,  28.37,   9.76,  15.06,  24.87,  18.40,  14.85,  16.22,  14.70,  15.79],  # S1\n        [ 13.30,  15.97,  12.06,  27.20,  16.70,  12.34,  21.49,  25.14,  12.47,  27.05,  19.42,  21.74,  17.29],  # S2\n        [ 13.19,   7.60,   7.56,   9.21,  29.17,   9.78,   8.38,  29.73,  18.84,  13.12,   9.55,  16.68,  12.79],  # S3\n        [ 18.77,   7.23,  11.41,  14.67,  22.24,  15.27,  27.12,  19.41,   9.24,  20.26,  27.96,  22.06,  24.49],  # S4\n        [ 23.42,   6.16,  19.64,  19.63,  18.34,  19.27,  21.40,  19.36,   8.01,  24.25,  26.55,  28.24,  24.42],  # S5\n        [ 13.94,  29.28,  24.97,  24.02,   9.13,  20.19,   8.28,  24.23,  13.26,  20.50,  13.16,  12.56,  10.90],  # S6\n        [  9.44,  13.51,  20.01,  11.78,   9.03,  22.30,  12.91,  13.75,  16.65,  28.90,  15.90,  23.58,  22.06],  # S7\n        [ 10.29,  14.73,  17.16,  12.39,  22.76,  23.36,  15.28,  25.42,  26.13,  25.63,  22.76,   8.44,  21.77],  # S8\n        [ 15.15,  29.88,   5.63,  28.66,  10.47,  26.29,  28.19,   9.59,  25.12,  20.68,  25.80,  14.24,  16.88],  # S9\n    ]\n\n    # Decision variables:\n    # Flow_S{i}_D{j} >= 0 is the quantity shipped from source i to destination j\n    flows = {}\n    for i in sources:\n        for j in destinations:\n            flows[(i, j)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Flow_S{i}_D{j}\")\n\n    # Objective: Minimize total transportation cost\n    m.setObjective(\n        quicksum(costs[i][j] * flows[(i, j)] for i in sources for j in destinations),\n        GRB.MINIMIZE\n    )\n\n    # Supply constraints: Shipments from each source <= its supply\n    for i in sources:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(flows[(i, j)] for j in destinations) <= supplies[i],\n            name=f\"Supply_S{i}\"\n        )\n\n    # Demand constraints: Shipments to each destination >= its demand\n    for j in destinations:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(flows[(i, j)] for i in sources) >= demands[j],\n            name=f\"Demand_D{j}\"\n        )\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
  "LLM_description": "Subject: Network shipping plan to meet demand at the lowest cost\nDate: [Date]\n\nSituation:\nOur network includes multiple source locations (warehouses and factories) supplying multiple destination locations (stores and customers). Customer service levels and freight spend are sensitive to how we allocate shipments across routes. Partial shipments are allowed, which gives us flexibility to split orders across lanes when it reduces cost or improves service.\n\nProblem:\nShipping costs vary by route, each source has limited inventory, and each destination has a required quantity to receive. Without a coordinated, data-driven plan, we risk stock imbalances, missed deliveries, and avoidable transportation expense. We need a clear allocation of shipments from each source to each destination that:\n- Does not exceed available inventory at any source\n- Meets the required quantity at every destination\n- Achieves the lowest total transportation cost across the network\n\nApproach:\n- Confirm the latest supply availability, destination requirements, and route-level shipping costs.\n- Develop a consolidated shipment allocation plan that leverages partial shipments where beneficial.\n- Validate feasibility with operations (lead times, dock capacity, carrier commitments, cut-off times).\n- Publish the recommended source-to-destination plan, with route assignments and an estimated cost summary.\n- Monitor execution and adjust as conditions change (inventory updates, demand shifts, carrier constraints).\n\nExpected outcome:\nA practical shipping plan that meets all demand requirements, stays within available inventory, and reduces overall freight spend while maintaining service levels.\n\nAnnex \u2013 Shipping Data:\nDestination requirements: Store D6 needs 41 units; Store D11 needs 67 units; Store D7 needs 43 units; Store D1 needs 33 units; Store D12 needs 21 units; Store D2 needs 72 units; Store D9 needs 60 units; Store D4 needs 16 units; Store D0 needs 